4],&quot;grossTop&quot;:[0,44948.144809266916],&quot;cleanShare&quot;:[0,0.12375874612639787],&quot;simplified&quot;:[0,0.8584905660377359],&quot;feeShare&quot;:[0,0.137311320754717]}],&quot;city&quot;:[0,&quot;Conway&quot;]}" ssr client="only" opts="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ProfitAdjuster&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;react&quot;}"></astro-island></div><p>To work out the profit on one Conway home, with its price, its mortgage or rent and your own costs, use the <a href="/calculator">Airbnb profit calculator</a>. It starts from the comparable listings around the address.</p><h3>How Conway's Top Earners Get There</h3><ul><li><strong>More nights booked.</strong> The busiest quarter of Conway listings are booked on 55% or more of their nights, against 36% for the median listing. Ten more booked nights a year at the median rate of $185 adds about $1,860 in bookings.</li><li><strong>Prices that follow demand.</strong> Ranked by price, the top quarter charge $285 a night or more, against a median of $185. That is a separate ranking from the busiest quarter, so the two marks don't multiply into one listing's takings. For the average listing, a 10% higher rate on the nights it already books adds about $2,050 a year.</li><li><strong>Open for the busy months.</strong> In a typical year, July brings the average listing about $3,850, against $1,550 in January, so a calendar that is open and full in the busy months carries the year.</li><li><strong>Reviews that stand out.</strong> Conway listings average 4.83 stars, and 48% carry Airbnb's Guest Favorite badge, which guests can filter for.</li></ul><p>What a listing keeps comes down to the figures this page measures: nightly rate, nights booked and the months it's open. A listing at the top-quarter mark takes in about $3,750 a month, against $1,950 for the average one.</p> </div> </section>  <section id="occupancy" class="mg-section mg-col"> <div class="mg-title mb-8"> <p class="font-lato text-[12px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[rgba(0,0,0,0.6)]"> Occupancy </p> <h2 class="mg-serif mt-1.5 text-[30px] font-bold leading-[1.12] sm:text-[36px] tracking-[-0.012em] text-[#1e293b]"> What Is the Airbnb Occupancy Rate in Conway? </h2>  </div> <div class="mg-report prose max-w-none">  <div id="monthly-occupancy"> <p>Conway listings were booked on <strong>36%</strong> of the nights they were open over the past year, 3 percentage points below the South Carolina average (39%) and 5 points below the U.S. average (41%). In a typical year, occupancy climbs to 51% in June and falls to 30% in February.</p><p>The busiest tenth of listings are booked about four times as often as the bottom quarter.</p><ul class="not-prose my-5 space-y-1.5"><li><span aria-hidden="true" class="mr-2.5 inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-[2px] align-[0.05em]" style="background-color:#4c8435"></span><span class="font-semibold text-[#1e293b]">Best-in-class properties</span> (top 10%) are booked <strong>72%+</strong> of open nights, 36 points above the median.</li><li><span aria-hidden="true" class="mr-2.5 inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-[2px] align-[0.05em]" style="background-color:#6ba559"></span><span class="font-semibold text-[#1e293b]">Strong performers</span> (top 25%) fill <strong>55%</strong> or more, roughly four nights a week.</li><li><span aria-hidden="true" class="mr-2.5 inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-[2px] align-[0.05em]" style="background-color:#afd89d"></span><span class="font-semibold text-[#1e293b]">Typical properties</span> (median) fill about <strong>36%</strong> of open nights.</li><li><span aria-hidden="true" class="mr-2.5 inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-[2px] align-[0.05em]" style="background-color:#d3eac8"></span><span class="font-semibold text-[#1e293b]">Entry-level properties</span> (bottom 25%) fill <strong>18%</strong> or less, under two nights a week.</li></ul><div class="not-prose my-8"><figure class="pseo-figure font-lato rounded-[4px] bg-white shadow-[0_1px_2px_rgba(15,23,42,0.06),0_3px_14