+See Every Little River Listing
+</span> </span> </a> </section> <section id="revenue" class="mg-section mg-col"> <div class="mg-title mb-8"> <p class="font-lato text-[12px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[rgba(0,0,0,0.6)]"> Revenue </p> <h2 class="mg-serif mt-1.5 text-[30px] font-bold leading-[1.12] sm:text-[36px] tracking-[-0.012em] text-[#1e293b]"> How Much Do Airbnb Hosts Make in Little River? </h2>  </div> <div class="mg-report prose max-w-none"> <p id="revenue-summary">Gross bookings per Little River listing averaged <strong>$14,963</strong> over the 12 months to September 2026 (South Carolina average: $37,525), before cleaning, platform and management costs and taxes.</p><div id="monthly-revenue"> <p>In a typical year, the average Little River listing brings in <strong>$3,650</strong> in July, its best month, and <strong>$1,300</strong> in November, its slowest. January runs within 3% of November, so either can be the slowest in a given year. The three strongest months bring in 40% of a full year's revenue, where an even calendar would give any three months 25%.</p><p>In a typical month, a top-quarter listing earns at least 3.5 times as much as a bottom-quarter one.</p><ul class="not-prose my-5 space-y-1.5"><li><span aria-hidden="true" class="mr-2.5 inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-[2px] align-[0.05em]" style="background-color:#0d47a1"></span><span class="font-semibold text-[#1e293b]">Best-in-class properties</span> (top 10%) earn <strong>$4,600+</strong> a month, about 2.7 times the typical property.</li><li><span aria-hidden="true" class="mr-2.5 inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-[2px] align-[0.05em]" style="background-color:#1976d2"></span><span class="font-semibold text-[#1e293b]">Strong performers</span> (top 25%) earn <strong>$3,000</strong> or more, roughly $1,300 a month above the median.</li><li><span aria-hidden="true" class="mr-2.5 inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-[2px] align-[0.05em]" style="background-color:#64b5f6"></span><span class="font-semibold text-[#1e293b]">Typical properties</span> (median) earn about <strong>$1,700</strong> a month.</li><li><span aria-hidden="true" class="mr-2.5 inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-[2px] align-[0.05em]" style="background-color:#bbdefb"></span><span class="font-semibold text-[#1e293b]">Entry-level properties</span> (bottom 25%) earn <strong>$854</strong> or less, about half of the median.</li></ul><p class="not-prose my-4 font-lato text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-[rgba(0,0,0,0.6)]">
