er the past year, about 44% below the South Carolina average of $355 and about 38% below the U.S. average of $320. In a typical year, rates peak in July at about $225 and bottom out in October and November at about $155.</p><p>The top 10% charge about 2.4 times the rate of the bottom quarter.</p><ul class="not-prose my-5 space-y-1.5"><li><span aria-hidden="true" class="mr-2.5 inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-[2px] align-[0.05em]" style="background-color:#5f5ab8"></span><span class="font-semibold text-[#1e293b]">Best-in-class properties</span> (top 10%) charge <strong>$310+</strong> a night, about 1.7 times the median.</li><li><span aria-hidden="true" class="mr-2.5 inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-[2px] align-[0.05em]" style="background-color:#8884d8"></span><span class="font-semibold text-[#1e293b]">Strong performers</span> (top 25%) charge <strong>$245</strong> or more, about $65 above the median.</li><li><span aria-hidden="true" class="mr-2.5 inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-[2px] align-[0.05em]" style="background-color:#b3b0e6"></span><span class="font-semibold text-[#1e293b]">Typical properties</span> (median) charge about <strong>$180</strong> a night.</li><li><span aria-hidden="true" class="mr-2.5 inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-[2px] align-[0.05em]" style="background-color:#dddcf5"></span><span class="font-semibold text-[#1e293b]">Entry-level properties</span> (bottom 25%) charge <strong>$130</strong> or less, about three-quarters of the median.</li></ul><div class="not-prose my-8"><figure class="pseo-figure font-lato rounded-[4px] bg-white shadow-[0_1px_2px_rgba(15,23,42,0.06),0_3px_14px_rgba(15,23,42,0.07)] p-5 sm:p-6 [&#38;_.pseo-table]:shadow-none"> <figcaption> <p class="text-[16px] font-bold leading-snug text-[#1e293b]">July rates run 43% above November&#39;s</p> <p class="mt-1 text-[14px] leading-snug text-[rgba(0,0,0,0.6)]">Average nightly rate (ADR), by month, September 2024 to August 2026</p>  </figcaption> <div class="mt-5"><div class="pseo-line r