t-lato text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-[rgba(0,0,0,0.6)]">Averages per active listing in each month. Highlighted: the highest-revenue month of the 12. RevPAR is the month&#39;s revenue spread over its nights, booked or not. Booking lead time is the days between booking and check-in, and length of stay the nights per booking, for stays in that month.</p> <p>For a figure on one home rather than the whole Pawleys Island market, enter its address and size in the <a href="/calculator">Airbnb income calculator</a>, which compares it with similar listings nearby.</p>  </div> </section>  <section id="profit" class="mg-section mg-col"> <div class="mg-title mb-8"> <p class="font-lato text-[12px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[rgba(0,0,0,0.6)]"> Profit </p> <h2 class="mg-serif mt-1.5 text-[30px] font-bold leading-[1.12] sm:text-[36px] tracking-[-0.012em] text-[#1e293b]"> Is an Airbnb in Pawleys Island Profitable? </h2>  </div> <div class="mg-report prose max-w-none"> <p id="profit-summary">Yes, when it's run well. The average Pawleys Island Airbnb took in <strong>$31,430</strong> in the 12 months to September 2026, and run by its owner at everyday costs, about <strong>$1,490 a month</strong> of that is left after running costs, so a home that costs less than that to own or rent makes money. A listing in the top quarter leaves about <strong>$2,590 a month</strong>.</p><p>Cleaning it yourself keeps the $5,440 a year guests pay in cleaning fees, for about $1,950 a month. Handing the listing to a co-host at about 10% of nightly bookings still leaves about $1,280 a month.</p><p>
+These amounts come before housing costs. Where the mortgage or rent is less each month, the difference is
+        profit; a home owned outright keeps it all after property tax, home insurance and any HOA or condo fees.
